{"id": "EUVD-2026-103059", "enisaUuid": "3e701c39-ffb2-34be-9e03-b3f1a0ec3daf", "description": "NexoPOS through 6.2.4 contains a missing authentication vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to read accounting transaction records via GET /api/fields/{resource}/{identifier}. Attackers can request transaction field classes like ns.entity-transaction with sequential ids to retrieve names, values, account ids, and descriptions without nexopos.read.transactions permission.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:12:40", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/nexopos-fields-endpoint-unauthenticated-transaction-disclosure", "https://github.com/Blair2004/NexoPOS/blob/v6.2.4/routes/api-base.php#L10-L18", "https://github.com/Blair2004/NexoPOS/blob/v6.2.4/app/Providers/FormsProvider.php#L126-L152", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nexopos-through-6.2.4-unauthenticated-transaction-disclosure-via-api-fields-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-222q-33hf-4cp6", "CVE-2026-111637"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14f0fa1b-2de8-3da7-8be5-0c574299a09a", "product": {"name": "NexoPOS", "vendor": {"name": "Blair2004"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "04268da8-747c-3cee-a263-10b23bd0c7f1", "vendor": {"name": "Blair2004"}}], "isExploited": false}